                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba768ce1-d657-3ec6-801c-4b41a7ba9c80",
                        "entry_id": "cc189298-8c5d-3664-ae27-0b4e01e6f474",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The speed of light (in vacuum unless another medium is specified)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1803ba70-8548-44e3-993c-e6bb327ac47c",
                                "sense_id": "ba768ce1-d657-3ec6-801c-4b41a7ba9c80",
                                "text": "If we're going to a world a hundred light-years from here at near lightspeed, we spend according to our own perceptions, only a few minutes doing so and arrive only a few minutes older."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1034a64a-9aeb-4e9d-a1b9-ba5cc76c66a3",
                                "sense_id": "ba768ce1-d657-3ec6-801c-4b41a7ba9c80",
                                "text": "He paused, then finished, “with the drive from the Linz, he can do over 500 lightspeeds to meet us."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f7e838a-672c-304a-a9d6-7675ced139aa",
                        "entry_id": "cc189298-8c5d-3664-ae27-0b4e01e6f474",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An extremely fast speed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "countable",
                            "figuratively",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e0a2b1b-d859-4ceb-b0d8-b1ce75818894",
                                "sense_id": "0f7e838a-672c-304a-a9d6-7675ced139aa",
                                "text": "In recent years, other activist terms have followed light-speed trajectories. The term “Latinx” overtook academic institutions and briefly became fashionable in the media, still prevalent in some influential publications, like The New Yorker, even though only 3 percent of Hispanics (or Latinos, if you prefer) use it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
